摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Git workspace enhancements for the DeepSeek Harness (dsh) Web GUI: worktree staging, sidebar git badges, files & diff conversation views, paseo-style PR actions","id":"gh:1361578487","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-better-workspaces","slug":"ds-hu/dsh-better-workspaces","topics":["ai-agent","code-review","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","diff-viewer","dsh","dsh-plugin","git","git-worktree","productivity","pull-request","web-gui","workspace-management","worktree"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Git workspace enhancements for the DeepSeek Harness (dsh) Web GUI: worktree staging, sidebar git bad"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ges, files & diff conversation views, paseo-style PR actions"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-better-workspaces"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English · 简体中文 · 日本語 · Français · 한국어"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Git worktrees, full diff inspection, pull requests, and issue references inside the DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" Web GUI. Give each task its own isolated branch and directory—navigate, review, and ship without sw"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"itching tabs or opening a terminal."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Plugin inventory name:** Better Workspaces · 工作区增强."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### 1. Workspace mode right in the composer"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Toggle between `Local` and `New worktree` directly above the prompt box. Keep simple edits in `Local"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"`; switch to `New worktree` whenever a task needs its own branch and isolated directory, preventing "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"parallel tasks from colliding."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"### 2. Fast branch setup from branches or PRs"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Enter a branch name or click the dice to generate one. Base your worktree on any local branch, remot"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"e branch, or open pull request. Clicking **Create** spins up an isolated workspace with a ready sess"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"n pull request. Clicking **Create** spins up an isolated workspace with a ready session immediately."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"### 3. Session status and diff size at a glance"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Every session card in the sidebar displays its active branch and diff volume (`+11 −3`). When a pull"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" request is open or CI checks are running, their status joins the same row—no need to run `git statu"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" CI checks are running, their status joins the same row—no need to run `git status` in the terminal."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"### 4. Full-page diff review in the sidebar"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Click the `±` badge to open the diff drawer. Switch smoothly across uncommitted changes, current ses"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"sion changes, task scope, or base branch comparisons. Expand hunks line-by-line, edit files in place"},{"id":"p14s3","text":", and inspect recent commits."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### 5. Git actions without leaving the page"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Run essential git actions straight from the diff view: Commit, Pull, Push, open a PR, merge, update "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"from base, or discard changes. Inapplicable actions clearly explain prerequisite states."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"### 6. Attach GitHub PRs and issues to prompts"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The GitHub button beside the composer lists open pull requests and issues from your repository. Sele"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ct any item to attach it directly to your prompt."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### 7. Compact composer chips, complete model context"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Prompts stay clean with a compact reference chip in the input box. On send, it automatically expands"},{"id":"p20s2","text":" into the full title, issue/PR body, branch details, and URL so the agent receives exact context."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Quick Workflow"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"1. **Start a session:** Open any git workspace in DeepSeek Harness.\n2. **Choose your scope:** Select"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" `Local` for quick in-place edits or `New worktree` for an isolated branch.\n3. **Develop & review:**"},{"id":"p22s3","text":" Use the GitHub picker to reference issues, check progress via sidebar badges, and click `±` to revi"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"ew line-by-line diffs.\n4. **Ship:** Commit, push, or open a pull request directly from the diff view"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"w line-by-line diffs.\n4. **Ship:** Commit, push, or open a pull request directly from the diff view."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Install from npm with one command:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Restart `dsh --profile web` once to activate."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Or install from the DSH Web GUI:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"1. Open **Plugins** in the sidebar.\n2. Click **Add plugin**.\n3. Enter `@ds-hu/dsh-better-workspaces`"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" and choose **Official npm registry** as the source.\n4. Click **Install**, then **Enable now** when "},{"id":"p28s3","text":"the installation finishes. If a restart is requested, restart `dsh --profile web`."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### Requirements\n- **DeepSeek Harness:** ≥ 0.2.0\n- **Node.js:** ≥ 20.19\n- **Tools:** `git`, `pnpm` ("},{"id":"p29s2","text":"available on `PATH`)\n- **GitHub CLI (optional):** Authenticated `gh` enables PR and issue picker fea"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"tures. Worktrees, sidebar badges, and diff review work fully without it."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Notes"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- Compatible with Linux, macOS 13+, and Windows 10+.\n- All operations run within the current browser"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"patible with Linux, macOS 13+, and Windows 10+.\n- All operations run within the current browser tab."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- docs/TECHNICAL.md — Architecture, design records, security model, upgrade notes, and manual operat"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"ions.\n- docs/adr/ — Architecture Decision Records detailing core design choices."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"MIT. Third-party notices and licenses are documented in NOTICE and LICENSES/."}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
